      "widgets_values": [
        "## Flux txt2img ultrawide 1536×640 (lab)\n\nWhat this graph does: Ultrawide cinematic text→image at 1536×640.\nModels: flux-2-klein-9b-nvfp4 + qwen_3_8b_fp4mixed (CLIP type flux2) + flux2-vae.\nSampler: euler · simple · CFG 1.0 · 8 steps · 1536×640 · batch 1\nSaveImage prefix: ez_flux_ultrawide.\n\nPrompting (Flux.2 Klein + Qwen3 TE):\n• Write natural-language prose, not SD tag soup. Subject first, then place, materials, lighting, camera.\n• Prefer positive constraints (“sharp focus”, “empty street”, “seamless white”) over “no X”.\n• Comfy (weight:1.4) emphasis is not applied by this text encoder.\n• At CFG 1.0 the Negative node is largely inert; quality is almost entirely the Positive prompt.\n\nHow to run:\n1. Review Positive prompt; queue."
      ],
